WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.460
Hi, I'm Nei Maldaner,

2
00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:02.820
and this is track two of the

3
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:03.720
LOOP-R course.

4
00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.120
You already ask AI for things every

5
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.800
day: proposals, replies to leads,

6
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:09.960
support messages.

7
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.700
But when someone asks whether things improved,

8
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:14.380
the answer is an impression.

9
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.500
This track solves that with a method

10
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.940
in five lessons:

11
00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:19.480
L for Locate,

12
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:20.680
O

13
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.200
for Operate, O

14
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.340
for Observe, P for Propose,

15
00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.000
and R for Reinforce.

16
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.200
You'll leave with your loop's goal written

17
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.080
as a number,

18
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.580
ten lines of evidence,

19
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:33.920
three testable hypotheses,

20
00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:35.960
and the criterion for deciding,

21
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:38.580
without guesswork, whether the new version won.

22
00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.840
We'll follow Marcos,

23
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.740
a real estate agent;

24
00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:42.440
Dr.

25
00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.800
Renata, owner of an aesthetics clinic;

26
00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:47.700
and Cláudio, who manages software support.

27
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:48.760
When I ask,

28
00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.420
pause and practice.

29
00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:51.700
The first letter is L,

30
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:52.810
for Locate.

31
00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:55.120
LOOP-R doesn't improve the whole company.

32
00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:57.120
It improves one process at a time:

33
00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.420
a task that happens at least dozens

34
00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:00.320
of times a month,

35
00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:02.040
has a clear beginning and end,

36
00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.060
and finishes with a result the person

37
00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:05.760
doing it can see.

38
00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.380
Marcos receives about eighty contacts a month

39
00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:09.920
from listing sites.

40
00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.720
Replying to the first contact is a

41
00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:13.800
process: it starts when a lead arrives

42
00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.600
and ends when they reply,

43
00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.500
or don't, within twenty-four hours.

44
00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.480
Negotiating fees and coordinating viewings belong to

45
00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:21.980
other loops.

46
00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:24.180
Think of renovating one room at a

47
00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:24.680
time.

48
00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:25.960
You finish the living room,

49
00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:27.580
then move on to the kitchen.

50
00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:29.380
Start with the room you use most,

51
00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:32.140
because that's where evidence builds fastest.

52
00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:34.020
The loop's goal has a fixed form:

53
00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.400
move a number from X to Y

54
00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.760
without worsening Z.

55
00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:38.280
From X is where you are today.

56
00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.140
To Y is a target you'd be

57
00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.580
glad to reach.

58
00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.940
And without worsening Z is the part

59
00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:46.500
almost everyone forgets.

60
00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:47.060
Dr.

61
00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:49.460
Renata sends proposals over WhatsApp after the

62
00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:50.080
assessment.

63
00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.480
Out of every hundred,

64
00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.560
three become paid packages.

65
00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:56.413
Her goal: move conversion from three to

66
00:01:56.413 --> 00:01:59.460
five percent without worsening average margin or

67
00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:00.720
increasing complaints.

68
00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.180
Why does the second half matter?

69
00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.700
Because one number alone becomes a target,

70
00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:07.980
and a system chasing a target learns

71
00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:08.760
to cheat.

72
00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:11.580
Without it, the version offering a twenty-percent

73
00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:14.080
discount would win every time.

74
00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:16.080
Cláudio wants to reduce service time without

75
00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.520
increasing tickets reopened within seven days.

76
00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:21.660
From X is the number you have

77
00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:22.160
today.

78
00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.520
If nobody tracks it,

79
00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.160
the first task is to count it.

80
00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.060
And it needs to answer quickly.

81
00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:30.440
Money metrics, such as conversion,

82
00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:31.700
take weeks.

83
00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:34.440
Signal metrics, such as whether a customer

84
00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:36.380
replied, show up in hours.

85
00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:38.760
To prove five versus

86
00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:39.840
three percent conversion,

87
00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.820
you need about fifteen hundred proposals per

88
00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:44.020
version.

89
00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:44.960
At Dr.

90
00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:46.520
Renata's pace of fifty a week,

91
00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.200
that takes more than a year.

92
00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.090
To prove the reply rate moved from

93
00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:50.960
twenty to thirty percent,

94
00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:53.140
about three hundred are enough:

95
00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:54.280
twelve weeks.

96
00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:56.460
That's why she tests replies and only

97
00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:57.700
monitors conversion.

98
00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:00.960
Marcos measures leads who reply within twenty-four

99
00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:04.700
hours: today, twenty-two out of every hundred.

100
00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:05.600
Pause:

101
00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:07.460
Cláudio wants fewer cancellations.

102
00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:09.440
Which number should he test first?

103
00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:11.460
The loop worksheet is the only thing

104
00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:11.960
you fill in.

105
00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:13.440
It has five questions,

106
00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:15.520
like the intake form at the clinic:

107
00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:16.580
you answer once,

108
00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:18.500
and the loop's assistants read it at

109
00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:19.800
every cycle.

110
00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.767
It doesn't promise conversion will reach five

111
00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:23.267
percent.

112
00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:26.160
It guarantees that no version that hurts

113
00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:28.680
margin or increases complaints becomes official,

114
00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.320
that everything is recorded,

115
00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:32.680
and that the cycle runs every week.

116
00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:34.440
Now pause the video for about ten

117
00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:34.980
minutes.

118
00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:37.920
List three processes that happen at least

119
00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:38.880
thirty times a month,

120
00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:40.820
and choose the one you repeat most.

121
00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.340
Write today's number,

122
00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:44.340
or “count first” if you don't know

123
00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:44.840
it.

124
00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:46.460
Write the target and at least one

125
00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:48.520
“without worsening.” Read it aloud.

126
00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.640
If it's longer than twenty-five words,

127
00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:51.720
cut

128
00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:52.420
it down.

129
00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:53.700
The second letter is O,

130
00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.220
for Operate: do the actual work.

131
00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:58.100
But just doing it however things turn

132
00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.820
out isn't enough.

133
00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:01.760
Marcos replied to leads from memory.

134
00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.560
On Monday, three paragraphs and a photo.

135
00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.700
On Thursday, in

136
00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:08.340
traffic, just “hi,

137
00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:09.380
interested?”

138
00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:12.120
Those were eighty executions of eighty different

139
00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:12.760
things.

140
00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:14.760
A written recipe can be wrong,

141
00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.560
and that's why it can be corrected.

142
00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.380
Nobody cooks exactly like Grandma every time.

143
00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:21.720
So the process gets a current version:

144
00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:24.800
a short written script followed in every

145
00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:25.640
execution.

146
00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.200
It doesn't need to be good;

147
00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.860
it needs to be one consistent version.

148
00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:32.300
The clinic's version one fit in six

149
00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:35.120
lines and produced two hundred comparable proposals

150
00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:35.960
in four weeks.

151
00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:36.900
First

152
00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:40.300
finding: one hundred sixty-six got no reply

153
00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.620
within forty-eight hours.

154
00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:44.080
If two executions differ in five things,

155
00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:45.640
you don't know which one made the

156
00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:46.840
difference.

157
00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:48.560
If they differ in one,

158
00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:49.620
you do.

159
00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:51.340
On Cláudio's support team,

160
00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:54.960
one agent sent step-by-step instructions with images,

161
00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.460
while another asked for remote access right

162
00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:58.047
away.

163
00:04:58.047 --> 00:05:00.860
Sixty-one percent were resolved on first contact.

164
00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:03.720
But sixty-one percent of what?

165
00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:04.940
A mixture.

166
00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:07.120
When both followed the same version one,

167
00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.800
the number fell to fifty-eight,

168
00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:10.520
and for the first time it meant

169
00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:11.460
something.

170
00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:13.120
Improvising isn't forbidden.

171
00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:15.220
Anyone who goes off script records it

172
00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:17.440
separately, and that row stays out of

173
00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:18.540
the comparison.

174
00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:21.050
So if Marcos followed the script for

175
00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:23.040
seventy leads and improvised on ten,

176
00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:25.180
he marks those ten and compares the

177
00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:25.860
other seventy.

178
00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:28.400
In LOOP-R, the assistant who executes has

179
00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:29.580
one job:

180
00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.080
the Executor.

181
00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:33.420
It receives the current version and the

182
00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:35.460
case data, produces the artifact,

183
00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:36.900
and records one row.

184
00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:37.900
It

185
00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:38.920
doesn't give opinions,

186
00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:41.200
make suggestions, or improve things on its

187
00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:41.700
own.

188
00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.460
The person who builds isn't the person

189
00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:45.940
who inspects; that's the method.

190
00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:47.700
An improvement made on the spot without

191
00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.700
a record is luck nobody can repeat.

192
00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.590
Now pause and practice.

193
00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:53.660
Marcos says it depends:

194
00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:55.760
sometimes he sends a photo and price

195
00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:59.400
right away, sometimes he asks first,

196
00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:01.760
sometimes he offers a viewing,

197
00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:03.740
and sometimes he forgets.

198
00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:04.660
Separate

199
00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:06.700
what he always does from what he

200
00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:07.760
does sometimes,

201
00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:10.120
then write his version one in up

202
00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:10.920
to six lines,

203
00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:14.140
choosing one fixed decision for each “sometimes.”

204
00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:15.800
Then do the same with your process.

205
00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:17.460
The third letter is O,

206
00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:18.620
for Observe.

207
00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:21.260
This is where the loop's intelligence begins,

208
00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:23.580
with an unglamorous step:

209
00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:25.720
every execution becomes a row,

210
00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:27.880
with its result recorded.

211
00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:29.020
At the clinic,

212
00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:31.153
the first two hundred proposals became two

213
00:06:31.153 --> 00:06:31.740
hundred rows.

214
00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:34.040
Adding up the “replied

215
00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:37.040
within forty-eight hours” column gave

216
00:06:37.535 --> 00:06:38.070
thirty-four.

217
00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:39.140
Seventeen percent.

218
00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:40.100
The

219
00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:41.180
worksheet said twenty,

220
00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:42.860
the number Dr.

221
00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:43.700
Renata had assumed.

222
00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:44.880
For the first time,

223
00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.820
the number left her head and went

224
00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:49.160
onto paper, and everything the loop proposes

225
00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:50.440
starts from seventeen.

226
00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:51.600
Think

227
00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:52.300
of blood pressure:

228
00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.400
the clinic doesn't ask whether you feel

229
00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:54.900
pressured.

230
00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:55.760
It

231
00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:57.220
measures, records,

232
00:06:57.240 --> 00:06:59.660
and compares with the last reading.

233
00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:02.680
The process log is an ordinary spreadsheet,

234
00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:05.000
the kind you already use.

235
00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:06.980
What changes is the discipline:

236
00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:08.620
one row per execution,

237
00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:10.400
always the same columns.

238
00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:13.080
The first columns say what

239
00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:16.680
and when: a code and the date.

240
00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:19.260
The middle ones say which version was

241
00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:20.900
followed and the variant,

242
00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:22.860
which stays A until there is a

243
00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:23.360
test.

244
00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:26.180
The last ones say what happened:

245
00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:28.340
replied, the quick metric;

246
00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:29.380
outcome,

247
00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:30.360
the money metric;

248
00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:31.300
and

249
00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.320
complained, the no-harm metric.

250
00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:35.420
Create the code when you execute.

251
00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:37.640
Leave the result blank and come back

252
00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:39.140
when the time window has passed.

253
00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:40.400
Answer yes or no,

254
00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:42.440
never “sort of.”

255
00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:44.280
If it can't be yes or no,

256
00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:45.960
the column isn't well defined.

257
00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:48.860
This spreadsheet is answer two on the

258
00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:49.500
worksheet.

259
00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:52.340
The assistants are the easy part.

260
00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:54.320
The hard part is that evidence lives

261
00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:55.700
in different places:

262
00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.620
WhatsApp, the listing site,

263
00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:58.600
the ticket system,

264
00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:00.360
or the salesperson's head.

265
00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:02.200
No assistant will fetch it on its

266
00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:02.700
own.

267
00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.600
Someone has to bring each result to

268
00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:05.100
the row.

269
00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:08.880
And every column needs a yes-or-no definition.

270
00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:10.440
On Cláudio's support team,

271
00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:13.360
resolved meant the customer did not reopen

272
00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:16.200
the ticket within seven days.

273
00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:17.560
At the clinic,

274
00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:20.220
replied meant a response within

275
00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:22.660
forty-eight hours that wasn't a refusal.

276
00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:23.960
Without that sentence,

277
00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:25.520
the version that prompts more “no,

278
00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:27.460
thank you” replies could

279
00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:29.480
look like the winner.

280
00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:32.180
If Marcos defines replied as any message

281
00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:34.380
back, even “stop messaging me” counts.

282
00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:37.340
Ten rows help you learn to fill

283
00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:39.740
it in; they don't support a conclusion.

284
00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:41.840
The loop only states a pattern with

285
00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:43.360
at least thirty rows of the same

286
00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:46.030
type, and calls the evidence strong at

287
00:08:46.030 --> 00:08:46.530
ninety.

288
00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:48.840
Below that, the observation goes on the

289
00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:49.840
“observed,

290
00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:50.840
not

291
00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:51.980
tested” list.

292
00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:53.340
With twelve leads,

293
00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:56.040
Marcos thought Tuesday leads replied more.

294
00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:57.160
Eight weeks later,

295
00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:59.240
with one hundred sixty rows,

296
00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:01.300
Tuesday was no different from any other

297
00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:01.800
day.

298
00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:04.600
Now pause and practice for about twelve

299
00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:05.600
minutes.

300
00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:08.280
Copy the headers into your spreadsheet and

301
00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:11.440
write the yes-or-no definition for each result

302
00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:12.200
column.

303
00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:14.280
Fill in your last ten executions,

304
00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:16.360
checking the source instead of relying on

305
00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:18.580
memory, and note where each result came

306
00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:19.240
from.

307
00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:21.180
Then decide who fills in the row

308
00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:22.207
and when.

309
00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:24.000
The fourth letter is P,

310
00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.160
for

311
00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:26.360
Propose.

312
00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:29.100
And proposing doesn't start with creativity.

313
00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:30.760
It starts with a cool reading of

314
00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:32.420
the spreadsheet by the Critic,

315
00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:34.240
an assistant with one job.

316
00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:35.560
It says what worked,

317
00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:38.020
what failed, and how strongly the evidence

318
00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:39.480
supports each statement.

319
00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:41.360
It doesn't suggest a solution.

320
00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:43.500
Looking at the clinic's two hundred proposals,

321
00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:45.310
it pointed out three things.

322
00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:48.200
One hundred sixty-six got no reply within

323
00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:49.640
forty-eight hours:

324
00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:50.660
eighty-three

325
00:09:50.660 --> 00:09:51.580
percent.

326
00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:52.880
Time was steady,

327
00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:54.580
about five and a half minutes per

328
00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:55.160
proposal.

329
00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:57.960
And version one ended with “available for

330
00:09:57.960 --> 00:10:00.500
any questions,” without asking the client to

331
00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:01.260
do anything.

332
00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:03.320
Three statements, three numbers,

333
00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:04.540
no suggestions.

334
00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:06.640
It's a mechanic's order:

335
00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:09.180
diagnosis first, estimate

336
00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:09.900
second.

337
00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:13.160
Whoever proposes before diagnosing may replace a

338
00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:13.660
good part.

339
00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:14.520
“Make

340
00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:16.780
the proposal shorter” is an idea,

341
00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:18.100
not a hypothesis.

342
00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:20.820
It can't be tested or rejected.

343
00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:23.880
A LOOP-R hypothesis has three parts.

344
00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:26.000
IF: what changes in the script.

345
00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:27.820
THEN: which number changes,

346
00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:29.320
and from what to what.

347
00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:32.500
BECAUSE: which evidence in the spreadsheet supports

348
00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:33.100
the bet.

349
00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:34.420
Then there's the CHANGE:

350
00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:36.060
the exact text to edit,

351
00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:38.420
so the Executor can follow it.

352
00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:39.180
Here's the clinic's,

353
00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:40.760
written by the Optimizer.

354
00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:42.860
IF the proposal

355
00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:44.700
has no more than eighty words,

356
00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:48.470
THEN the reply rate should rise from

357
00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:51.540
seventeen to at least twenty-two percent,

358
00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:52.500
BECAUSE

359
00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:55.180
eighty-three percent don't reply and the five-block

360
00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:57.120
message is long for WhatsApp.

361
00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:00.160
CHANGE: add an eighty-word maximum to the

362
00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:01.100
rules.

363
00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:02.300
This one can fail.

364
00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.300
An idea that cannot fail a test

365
00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:06.300
cannot improve anything either.

366
00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:09.140
The Critic labels the strength of each

367
00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:10.340
statement:

368
00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:12.620
strong with ninety rows or more,

369
00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:14.160
moderate from thirty,

370
00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:15.980
and weak below that.

371
00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:17.900
Since only one thing is tested at

372
00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:19.980
a time, strong hypotheses go first,

373
00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:22.980
and weak ones wait on the “observed,

374
00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:24.280
not tested” list.

375
00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:25.860
Marcos had two ideas.

376
00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:27.660
One came from twenty-five leads:

377
00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:29.300
weak, so it waited.

378
00:11:29.300 --> 00:11:30.720
The other came from one hundred thirty

379
00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:33.540
rows, one hundred one without a reply:

380
00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:34.280
strong.

381
00:11:34.280 --> 00:11:35.680
It became the test.

382
00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:37.520
IF the first reply ends with one

383
00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:40.020
clear question, such as “Would you prefer

384
00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:42.040
to visit this week or next?”,

385
00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:44.780
THEN the twenty-four-hour reply rate will rise

386
00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:48.040
from twenty-two to at least twenty-eight percent,

387
00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:49.240
BECAUSE

388
00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:52.360
the current text doesn't ask for a

389
00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:52.860
reply.

390
00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:55.120
A hypothesis isn't

391
00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:56.060
a rule yet.

392
00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:58.360
It passes through two gates.

393
00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:00.540
First is the Guardian:

394
00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:02.640
if the change touches something that must

395
00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:03.880
never change on its own,

396
00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:06.840
or puts a no-harm metric at risk,

397
00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:08.320
the Guardian vetoes it,

398
00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:10.120
and that veto is final.

399
00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:12.460
The second gate is the test.

400
00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:13.980
Cláudio's hypothesis,

401
00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:15.140
three

402
00:12:15.140 --> 00:12:16.880
steps to the payment screen,

403
00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:17.460
passed.

404
00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:18.360
At

405
00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:20.740
the clinic, the single closing question,

406
00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:22.080
the same one Marcos used,

407
00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:24.220
was vetoed because Dr.

408
00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:27.020
Renata's worksheet had zero tolerance for complaints.

409
00:12:27.020 --> 00:12:29.660
The Guardian reads each loop's worksheet.

410
00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:30.860
Now pause.

411
00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:32.960
Paste the Optimizer prompt from the lesson

412
00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:34.220
into your AI chat,

413
00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:35.240
with your data,

414
00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:38.000
and ask for three hypotheses with IF,

415
00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:40.020
THEN, BECAUSE, and CHANGE.

416
00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:41.060
With ten rows,

417
00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:42.200
they'll all be weak,

418
00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:42.960
and that's right.

419
00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:46.140
Then play the Guardian and cross out

420
00:12:46.140 --> 00:12:49.140
any hypothesis that touches something that never

421
00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:49.960
changes.

422
00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:51.740
The fifth letter is R,

423
00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:54.100
for Reinforce: test,

424
00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:55.180
evaluate,

425
00:12:55.180 --> 00:12:58.300
and only then incorporate or discard.

426
00:12:58.300 --> 00:13:00.960
Marcos read twenty replies using

427
00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:01.980
the new version,

428
00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:04.500
liked them, and wanted to change the

429
00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:05.440
script that day.

430
00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:06.900
He had an impression,

431
00:13:06.900 --> 00:13:08.360
but no outcome recorded.

432
00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:09.620
In the test,

433
00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:11.740
half the executions follow the current version,

434
00:13:11.740 --> 00:13:13.560
A, and half

435
00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:14.140
the candidate, B,

436
00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:17.100
during the same randomly assigned weeks.

437
00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:19.520
The Experimenter calculates the amount needed for

438
00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:21.720
proof, estimates the number of weeks,

439
00:13:21.720 --> 00:13:23.660
and writes the stopping rule before the

440
00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:24.640
test starts.

441
00:13:24.640 --> 00:13:25.700
Why together?

442
00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:27.720
December has holidays at the clinic,

443
00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:29.240
January has vacations,

444
00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:31.900
and replies shift by eight points without

445
00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:33.060
anyone changing anything.

446
00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:34.040
If

447
00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:36.320
Marcos ran A in August and B

448
00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:38.600
in September, he couldn't separate the script

449
00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:39.660
from the calendar.

450
00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:42.060
The Evaluator reads the spreadsheet and gives

451
00:13:42.060 --> 00:13:43.380
one of three answers.

452
00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:46.240
B won: the difference is bigger than

453
00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:47.860
chance can explain,

454
00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:49.840
the required amount has been reached,

455
00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:52.600
and no no-harm metric fell beyond its

456
00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:53.680
allowed margin.

457
00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:56.060
A stays: B didn't win,

458
00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:57.940
or it won on the main number

459
00:13:57.940 --> 00:13:59.880
but lost on a guardrail.

460
00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:01.020
Not enough data:

461
00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:02.000
keep testing.

462
00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:04.100
There is no “it's winning.” That's the

463
00:14:04.100 --> 00:14:04.840
most common answer.

464
00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:06.750
After three weeks,

465
00:14:06.750 --> 00:14:08.780
Cláudio's B resolved

466
00:14:08.953 --> 00:14:10.860
sixty-six percent on first contact,

467
00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:12.540
versus sixty-one for A.

468
00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:13.900
He wanted to stop.

469
00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:16.300
The Evaluator said not enough data:

470
00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:18.460
the worksheet required two hundred twenty tickets

471
00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:20.940
per version, and there were only sixty-two.

472
00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:23.060
Stopping early because it's winning is the

473
00:14:23.060 --> 00:14:24.400
most common way to make a difference

474
00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:26.480
that doesn't exist official.

475
00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:29.780
B only wins if the number rises

476
00:14:29.780 --> 00:14:32.680
and no no-harm metric falls beyond the

477
00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:33.380
worksheet's tolerance.

478
00:14:33.380 --> 00:14:35.260
Both conditions must hold.

479
00:14:35.260 --> 00:14:37.000
At the end of Cláudio's test,

480
00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:40.047
first-contact resolution rose from fifty-eight to sixty-six

481
00:14:40.047 --> 00:14:40.547
percent.

482
00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:43.420
But tickets reopened within seven days rose

483
00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:44.900
from four to nine percent,

484
00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:47.500
with a tolerance of two points.

485
00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:48.160
A stays.

486
00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:51.580
B resolved tickets by closing ones that

487
00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:53.580
came back, the very trick the no-harm

488
00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:55.400
metric was there to catch.

489
00:14:55.400 --> 00:14:56.940
For frequent numbers,

490
00:14:56.940 --> 00:14:58.400
zero tolerance works.

491
00:14:58.400 --> 00:14:59.660
For rare events,

492
00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:01.240
like one complaint in a hundred,

493
00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:03.940
zero can't separate an effect from chance.

494
00:15:03.940 --> 00:15:06.060
Tolerance has to cover the noise:

495
00:15:06.060 --> 00:15:08.487
about one point for one-percent events in

496
00:15:08.487 --> 00:15:09.700
three hundred rows.

497
00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:11.360
Zero there rejects

498
00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:12.880
good hypotheses by chance.

499
00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:13.980
When B wins,

500
00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:15.900
the decision still goes through you.

501
00:15:15.900 --> 00:15:17.180
At most once a week,

502
00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:18.840
you get a five-line card with three

503
00:15:18.840 --> 00:15:20.720
buttons: approve, reject,

504
00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:22.360
or wait for more data.

505
00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:24.300
If you don't respond by the deadline,

506
00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:25.360
it doesn't become official.

507
00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:28.400
Once approved, the candidate becomes the current

508
00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:31.140
version, and the old one stays in

509
00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:33.520
the history with a rollback button.

510
00:15:33.520 --> 00:15:35.340
If any number falls below the old

511
00:15:35.340 --> 00:15:37.720
version's result during the first cycle after

512
00:15:37.720 --> 00:15:39.500
the change, it goes back.

513
00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:40.380
At the clinic,

514
00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:43.160
version two, which mentions one detail from

515
00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:44.140
the client's assessment,

516
00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:47.284
raised replies from nineteen point three to

517
00:15:47.284 --> 00:15:48.260
twenty-nine point three percent,

518
00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:50.940
with the guardrails within tolerance.

519
00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:53.960
Conversion was three point seven versus three,

520
00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:55.060
a

521
00:15:55.060 --> 00:15:57.960
difference three hundred proposals can't prove.

522
00:15:57.960 --> 00:16:00.900
The loop delivered what it promised.

523
00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:02.900
Pause and give the verdict for about

524
00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:04.040
ten minutes.

525
00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:05.840
The clinic's second cycle,

526
00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:08.080
testing the eighty-word hypothesis.

527
00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:10.040
A versus B during the same twelve

528
00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:12.340
weeks, three hundred proposals each,

529
00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:15.460
and the worksheet required one hundred sixty-six.

530
00:16:15.460 --> 00:16:17.380
Replies within forty-eight hours:

531
00:16:17.380 --> 00:16:18.980
A, nineteen point three;

532
00:16:18.980 --> 00:16:19.916
B,

533
00:16:19.916 --> 00:16:21.260
twenty-nine point seven percent.

534
00:16:21.260 --> 00:16:22.280
Complaints,

535
00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:23.960
with zero tolerance:

536
00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:24.920
A had one,

537
00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:27.000
B had six out of three hundred.

538
00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:29.460
Margin and requests to stop were within

539
00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:30.080
limits.

540
00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:32.180
Which of the three answers?

541
00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:33.780
A stays.

542
00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:35.840
B won on the main number by

543
00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:36.620
a wide margin,

544
00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:39.160
but complaints exceeded the written tolerance.

545
00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:40.760
And the rule?

546
00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:42.580
Complaints are rare events,

547
00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:45.540
so zero tolerance was poorly written.

548
00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:46.940
Set it to one point for future

549
00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:47.660
tests.

550
00:16:47.660 --> 00:16:49.880
This test is not rejudged.

551
00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:52.200
Changing the yardstick after seeing the result

552
00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:54.120
is how you promote something because it

553
00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:54.780
seems better.

554
00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:57.100
You've completed the five letters.

555
00:16:57.100 --> 00:16:59.720
Locate gave you one process and one

556
00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:03.060
number, with the no-harm condition protecting the

557
00:17:03.060 --> 00:17:03.840
business.

558
00:17:03.840 --> 00:17:06.500
Operate gave you a written version that

559
00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.200
makes executions comparable.

560
00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:10.753
Observe turned executions into

561
00:17:10.753 --> 00:17:11.620
yes-or-no rows.

562
00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:14.240
Propose brought hypotheses that can fail a

563
00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:15.420
test.

564
00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:18.000
And Reinforce taught you to give a

565
00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:19.060
verdict by the rule,

566
00:17:19.060 --> 00:17:21.900
even with ten points screaming the opposite.

567
00:17:21.900 --> 00:17:24.340
One last step for your work:

568
00:17:24.380 --> 00:17:27.420
reread the no-harm condition in answer one

569
00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:30.310
and write the tolerance for each metric.

570
00:17:30.310 --> 00:17:31.620
For rare events,

571
00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:33.960
replace zero with one point.

572
00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:34.900
In track three,

573
00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:37.040
you'll meet the nine single-purpose assistants:

574
00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:38.540
who executes, observes,

575
00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:39.720
critiques, and vetoes,

576
00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:41.500
and why none can do another's job

577
00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:43.600
without the loop starting to convince itself.
